---
import LocalNav from '../components/LocalNav.astro';
import EventFooter from '../components/EventFooter.astro';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-IN" dir="ltr">
    <head>
        <meta charset="utf-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
        <title>Terms &amp; Conditions - AAAI Event Hub</title>
        <meta name="Description" content="Terms and conditions for attending the AAAI Event Hub — passes, refunds, code of conduct, liability and more." />
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/fonts.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/ac-localnav.built.css" />
        <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/css/event-pages.css" />
    </head>
    <body>
        <LocalNav current="terms" />
        <main class="event-main">
            <header class="event-hero">
                <p class="eyebrow">AAAI Event Hub</p>
                <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions.</h1>
                <p class="subhead">The short, fair rules that keep the event running smoothly for everyone.</p>
            </header>

            <section class="event-section on-white" aria-label="Terms and conditions">
                <div class="event-container prose">
                    <p class="prose-meta">Last updated: 1 January 2026</p>

                    <h2>1. Passes</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li>A pass grants entry to one person for all event days and is non-transferable after badge collection, except through an approved transfer before the event.</li>
                        <li>Student passes require a valid student ID presented at registration.</li>
                        <li>We may refuse entry or revoke a pass for breach of these terms or the code of conduct, without refund.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h2>2. Refunds &amp; transfers</h2>
                    <p>Full refunds are available up to 14 days before the event. Within 14 days, no refunds are issued but you may transfer your pass free of charge by emailing the attendee's details to <a href="mailto:passes@aaaihub.org">passes@aaaihub.org</a>.</p>

                    <h2>3. Programme changes</h2>
                    <p>Speakers, venues and session times may change due to circumstances beyond our control. We will communicate changes via email and on this website as early as possible.</p>

                    <h2>4. Code of conduct</h2>
                    <p>All attendees, speakers, sponsors and staff must follow our code of conduct. Harassment or disruptive behaviour of any kind leads to removal from the venue without refund.</p>

                    <h2>5. Photography &amp; recording</h2>
                    <p>Personal photography is welcome unless signage or staff indicate otherwise. Commercial recording of sessions is reserved for authorised media partners.</p>

                    <h2>6. Liability</h2>
                    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the organiser's total liability arising out of or relating to attendance is limited to the value of your pass. Personal belongings remain your responsibility at all times.</p>

                    <h2>7. Force majeure</h2>
                    <p>If the event cannot be held due to events beyond our reasonable control (including natural disasters, government restrictions or public-health measures), we will offer either a transfer of your pass to a rescheduled date or a pro-rata refund.</p>

                    <h2>8. Governing law</h2>
                    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India, with courts in Mumbai having exclusive jurisdiction.</p>

                    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
                    <p>Questions about these terms? Write to <a href="mailto:hello@aaaihub.org">hello@aaaihub.org</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </section>
        </main>
        <EventFooter />
    </body>
</html>
